{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To start, you should join the team and agree on the team's domain."
      ],
      "justification": "Process start and initial team-joining step correspond directly to the opening unit."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2",
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once that is done, create a process model and check it."
      ],
      "justification": "Model creation and checking are split into two actions. Checking a condition is re-typed as an action step, which preserves behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the process model is \"NOT OK\", then assign negative points."
      ],
      "justification": "First decision split and negative outcome. Guard v1=false correctly captures the NOT OK condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n7",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the process is okay, you can continue with it."
      ],
      "justification": "Positive branch from the first check. Guard v1=true captures the okay condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5",
        "guard:b2->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If it is still \"NOT OK\", assign negative points again."
      ],
      "justification": "Second decision split and negative outcome. Condition is modeled as an action (n5) before the branch, which is an acceptable re-typing."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the process is okay, you can continue with it."
      ],
      "justification": "Positive branch from the second check, preserving the continuation path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there are any issues, fix them in the next session and extend the process to levels 2 and 3."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of the issue-fixing and extension step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If you need to check the process and assign points, continue with the process.",
        "If you need to analyze the field of study, assign roles in the team."
      ],
      "justification": "Combines the two conditional requirements into a single action description. Merging equivalent preconditions preserves behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If you need to analyze the field of study, assign roles in the team."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicitly models the role assignment step referenced in the second condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the process is okay, continue with the process and perform work according to your assigned role."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the core work-performing step. Flow continuation is implicit in the sequence."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n18"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Check the progress and consult any problems that arise."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of the monitoring step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n19",
        "guard:b5->n20",
        "guard:b5->n21",
        "action:n20",
        "action:n21"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the project is accepted, present it. If not, continue working according to your role."
      ],
      "justification": "First acceptance check and both branches are fully captured. Guards v3=true/false correctly align with accepted/not."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n22",
        "guard:b6->n23",
        "guard:b6->n24",
        "action:n23",
        "action:n24"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the project is accepted, present it again. If not, continue working according to your role."
      ],
      "justification": "Second acceptance check and both branches are fully captured. Guards v4=true/false correctly align with accepted/not."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n25"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, present the project and the process will come to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Final presentation step and process termination correspond exactly."
    }
  ],
